-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",58,{
[1825]="700682DB\n1\tCollect stolen supplies (total: 8)\tKiria asked you to retrieve any stolen goods to which the bog-lurkers may have taken a liking. They can be found at Basha Ghând to the north-west.\n2\tTalk to Kiria\tYou seem to have collected all of the supplies that the bog-lurkers lifted from Kiria. You should return to Kiria. Kiria can be found in Mâr Naphra.\n",
[1826]="70051640\n1\tDefeat Bogbereth\tBogbereth hunts in the north-east reaches of Himbar, west and then north of Gath Forthnír. Lunathron cautioned you not to face Bogbereth with anything less than a fully-armed war-party. She must be defeated, lest she continues to spawn more of her foul brood.\n2\tTalk to Lunathron\tGath Forthnír is in the eastern part of Himbar, south and east of Torech-i-Bogbereth. Lunathron bade you destroy the great spider, Bogbereth. Now that she is no more, you can return to claim your victory.\n",
[1827]="70000198\n1\tDefeat Bogbereth's broodlings (total: 10)\030Defeat matrons, lurkers, and creepers (total: 5)\tThe spiders are to the north-east of Himbar. Lunathron told you of Bogbereth's spawn, the spider-broodlings that are kept by the Angmarim.\n2\tTalk to Lunathron\tLunathron is at Gath Forthnír, to the east of Himbar. You slew many spiders and their Angmarim keepers, ensuring that Bogbereth's spawn pose no threat to the Rangers. Now you should return to Lunathron.\n",
[1828]="70017B8C\n1\tSpeak to Hadi to find out what he knows\tHadi resides in camp with Folkath at the west edge of the Fanged Pit. Folkath recommends that you question Hadi about what he has learned of Bogrian's clan.\n2\tSpy upon and defeat two scouts (total: 2)\tSeek out the scouts at their habitual meeting-place, south of the entrance to Tith-maudhul, and try to overhear their conversation before you defeat them.\n3\tTalk to Folkath at his camp in the Fanged Pit\tFolkath is at the camp on the west edge of the Fanged Pit. You should return to Folkath with news of your success.\n",
[1829]="70026EF6\n1\tDefeat wolves in Trum Dreng (total: 10)\tWolves roam the rocky plains south of Lhan Tarren. You should slay wolves for the protection and well-being of the Stag-clan.\n2\tTalk to Guto at Lhan Tarren\tGuto holds his post at Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan in Trum Dreng. You should speak with Guto and tell him that you slew many wolves while roaming the wilds beyond the village.\n",
[1830]="700080F7\n1\tBring the collected materials to [see journal]\030Collect the barrel of nails\030Collect the crate of hammers\030Collect the crate of saws\tThe stolen supplies can be found in the Orc camps to the north-east. Elsie told you that the outlying farmers were supposed to be bringing some of the supplies she needs -- specifically a barrel of nails, a crate of hammers, and a crate of saws -- but their farms were overrun and their goods stolen. She has asked you to go to the Orc camps north along the Greenway and gather the supplies the Orcs scattered.\n",
[1831]="7004E4EF\n1\tAcquire Dalish medicine\tDalish medicine can be found inside Utterby. You should find the Dalish medicine.\n2\tTreat ill refugees (total: 6)\tIll refugees can be found inside Utterby. You should offer medicine to ill refugees.\n3\tTalk to Tuhâl\tYou should talk to Tuhâl, who can be found in Utterby.\n",
[1832]="70048F7E\n1\tDefeat Bolvág the Cursed\tBolvág the Cursed can be found patrolling Mordor. You have encountered the threatening Bolvág the Cursed. Roaming the poisonous realm of Agarnaith, the beast patrols the dreadful terrain with his deformed minions.\n2\tDefeat Bolvág the Cursed\tBolvág the Cursed can be found patrolling Mordor. You have encountered the threatening Bolvág the Cursed. Roaming the poisonous realm of Agarnaith, the beast patrols the dreadful terrain with his deformed minions.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Bolvág the Cursed.\n",
[1833]="70036B35\n1\tDefeat the goblin-sappers ([see journal]/12)\tStop the goblin-sappers from destroying the barricades, supply crates, and the large crystal clusters at the end of the island bridge. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[1834]="700380E7\n1\tDefeat the goblin-sappers ([see journal]/20)\tStop the goblin-sappers from destroying the barricades, supply crates, and the large crystal clusters at the end of the island bridge. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[1835]="700216ED\n1\tCollect fake Bombur's Beard Lager from The Green Dragon\tBarmy Rootknot is at The Green Dragon in Bywater. You should speak with Barmy Rootknot and collect some Dragon's Breath Ale, which will be delivered to poor Múli in place of his beloved Bombur's Beard Lager.\n2\tBring the fake Bombur's Beard Lager to Múli\tMúli is at Othrikar in the North Downs. You should deliver the Dragon's Breath Ale to Múli in place of his beloved Bombur's Beard Lager.\n",
[1836]="7005A803\n1\tTalk to Thromur\tThromur can be found at Amdân. Thromur, esquire of Frerin, has asked you to accompany him to confront Shálun. You should talk to Thromur.\n2\tTalk to Thromur at Durin's Stone\tThromur can be found at Durin's Stone. You have aided in the defeat of Urro One-hand and routed Bolg and the other Orcs at Durin's Stone. You should talk to Thromur.\n",
[1837]="700033F3\n1\tDefeat the Bone Man\tThe shade does not know precisely where the Bone Man may be found, other than that he lies somewhere in the south Barrow-downs. The shade spoke of the Bones of a man of Cardolan returned to life and of the oath he and his brother made.\n2\tTalk to the Wandering Shade\tThe shade wanders through the northern Barrow-downs. You should return to the shade and let him know that the Bone Man has been defeated and the shades freed.\n",
[1838]="7000F0C9\n1\tTalk to Tulk\tTulk is east of the ruined gate near the Walls of Moria, in the south-east of Eregion. Ráthwald has told you that an expedition of dwarves has come to Hollin to seek out Balin within the halls of Khazad-dûm. He has told you to offer your aid to Tulk just beyond the ruined gate where he keeps watch.\n",
[1839]="70000137\n1\tFind and defeat the crebain and their master\tThe Barrow-downs are reached by going north and east along the Old Barrows Road. The crebain stopped to roost in the trees within the Barrow-downs, south along the ridge, above the eaves of the forest. Tom Bombadil found the crebain within the Barrow-downs, but also mentioned the presence of a woman. You should stay on your guard.\n2\tTalk to Tom Bombadil at his house\tThe Old Barrows Road is north of Andraste's grove. The house of Tom Bombadil is west and south along the Old Barrows Road. Andraste revealed that the Lord of the Nazgûl had gone to someplace called Othrongroth, but you could learn nothing more before her death. Tom Bombadil is the Master of the Wood and of the Barrow-downs. He might know where Othrongroth lies.\n",
[1840]="7003FDDC\n1\tTalk to Pethebir in the library of Dol Amroth\tPethebir is at the libraries of Dol Amroth. Lothíriel believes the best way to prepare for the threat of the Corsairs of Umbar is to learn as much about their ways as you can, and to that end she has sent you to the libraries of Dol Amroth.\n2\tTalk to Naremil and learn about Gondor\030Talk to Cirhael and learn about Umbar\030Talk to Nosseth and learn about Prince Imrahil and Lothíriel\tPethebir has given you the names of several scholars who may be able to help you.\n3\tTalk to Pethebir\tPethebir is at the libraries of Dol Amroth. Lothíriel believes the best way to prepare for the threat of the Corsairs of Umbar is to learn as much about their ways as you can, and to that end she has sent you to the libraries of Dol Amroth.\n4\tTalk to Lothíriel\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. You have learned that Lothíriel is unhappily betrothed to her cousin Boromir, and should tell her of her intended's fate.\n",
[1841]="70061BD5\n1\tTalk to Meneldir at Idhobel\tMeneldir is at the camp of Idhobel, in Western Eregion.\n2\tReturn to Skardí Bendblade's blacksmith shop in Mossward\tMeneldir has recommended that you return to Skardí Bendblade's blacksmith shop in Mossward so you can restock and resupply for your journey north to Meneldir's kin.\n3\tTalk to Skardí Bendblade in his blacksmith shop in Mossward\tSkardí Bendblade stands behind the counter of his blacksmith shop in Mossward.\n",
[1842]="70000138\n1\tSpeak to Tom Bombadil\tTom Bombadil has agreed to show you the way to Othrongroth, a barrow in the Barrow-downs.\n2\tTalk to Tom Bombadil\tReturn to Tom Bombadil and claim your reward. You and your allies braved the dark depths of Othrongroth and emerged victorious.\n",
[1843]="70061BEC\n1\tTalk to Meneldir in the blacksmith shop in Mossward\tMeneldir stands inside Skardí Bendblade's blacksmith shop in Mossward, considering your next steps.\n2\tMeet up with Meneldir on the southern bank of the Gwathló, north-west of Mossward\tMeneldir advised that you consider the crossing of the Gwathló at Tharbad very carefully: the river has a dangerous reputation where it passes through the city.\n3\tTalk to the woman at the crossing of the Gwathló\tYou encountered a woman of Rohan on the southern bank of the Gwathló. The woman looks at you curiously from the back of her steed.\n4\tTalk to Meneldir at the crossing of the Gwathló\tMeneldir stands on the southern bank of the Gwathló, considering how best to answer the woman of Rohan you encountered.\n5\tTalk to the woman at the crossing of the Gwathló\tThe woman of Rohan stands on the southern bank of the Gwathló, reluctant to be parted from her steed.\n6\tReach the halfway point of the crossing of Gwathló\tThe crossing of the Gwathló has been perilous for many years, ever since the flooding of the bridge and the loss of a safe road through Tharbad.\n7\tSwim to the other side of the perilous river Gwathló\tThe crossing of the Gwathló has been perilous for many years, ever since the flooding of the bridge and the loss of a safe road through Tharbad.\n8\tTalk to Meneldir on the northern bank of the Gwathló\tMeneldir has made the crossing, and stands exhausted on the northern bank.\n9\tWait for Egfrith to join you on the northern bank of the Gwathló\tEgfrith has almost made it across the Gwathló.\n10\tTalk to Egfrith on the northern bank of the Gwathló\tEgfrith has successfully made the crossing.\n",
[1844]="7003FDDD\n1\tTalk to Nedhros on Amon Lontir, in Belfalas\tNedhros is on the hill of Amon Lontir, by the great beacon. Lothíriel has sent you to recall Nedhros, the swan-knight she sent out of the city into the lands of Belfalas.\n2\tTalk to Heledir by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon\tHeledir is by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon. Lothíriel has sent you to recall the Swan-knight Heledir, currently scouting on her behalf in Lamedon.\n3\tFind the hidden villain near the beacon of Maegond\tSome villain is hidden atop the hill by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon. Heledir has agreed to return to Dol Amroth, but has asked you to seek out the hidden villain he sensed near the beacon of Maegond.\n4\tFind and defeat the Corsair leader near the beacon of Maegond\tSome villain is hidden atop the hill by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon. Heledir has agreed to return to Dol Amroth, but has asked you to seek out the hidden villain he sensed near the beacon of Maegond.\n5\tFind and talk to Rovalang somewhere in the Blackroot Vale\tRovalang was near the Hill of Erech, in Blackroot Vale, when last you saw him. Lothíriel asked you to find Rovalang, the swan-knight she sent to Blackroot Vale.\n",
[1845]="70000139\n1\tTalk to Strider\tStrider awaits your return in his room at The Prancing Pony in Bree. The entrance leading from the Barrow-downs to the Great East Road is to the north. Travel back to Bree and tell Strider what you learned of the Witch-king's plans.\n2\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur\tBarliman Butterbur serves his guests in the common room of The Prancing Pony. You travelled back to The Prancing Pony, but you found the door to Strider's room locked. You should speak to Barliman Butterbur to learn if he can tell you where Strider has gone.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf\tGandalf's room in The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree is found by taking a left out of the common room, until you can only bear right. The room is at the top of the stairs at the end of the hall. Barliman Butterbur told you that Strider has left The Prancing Pony, but that Gandalf, a Wizard by reputation, arrived and asked to speak to any who were looking for the Ranger. You should speak to Gandalf and tell him what you have learned.\n",
[1846]="7003FDE2\n1\tTalk to Rovalang and face 'The Shadow in Morthond'\tRovalang is on the slopes of the Hill of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale. The Nazgûl must be prevented from learning of Aragorn's passage with the army of the Dead, at any cost.\n2\tTalk to Rovalang on the Hill of Erech, in Blackroot Vale\tRovalang is on the slopes of the Hill of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale. With the help of Rovalang, you have driven off the Nazgûl that threatened to learn of Aragorn's passage with the army of the Dead.\n3\tTalk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. You faced a Nazgûl in the Blackroot Vale, and though it has been driven away formless to its master, this is a clear sign that the Great Enemy has Gondor much on his mind.\n",
[1847]="700579E6\n1\tTalk to Rodwen in the throne room of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tRodwen the wedding-planner is in the throne room of Minas Tirith as Midsummer's Day approaches. The name is familiar, but the Rodwen you met was an adventurer who ran into trouble along the East Wall of Rohan in the company of her friends, and not a planner of weddings. You may use stable-masters at major towns and cities to advance to Minas Tirith (Midsummer) for the wedding festivities.\n2\tTalk to Rodwen up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tRodwen is up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Rodwen has asked to meet you outside the throne room, and away from listening ears. For what purpose does the expert wedding-planner seek this secret meeting?\n",
[1848]="700579E7\n1\tTalk to Rodwen the wedding-planner in the throne room of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tRodwen the wedding-planner is in the throne room of Minas Tirith as Midsummer's Day approaches. You may use stable-masters at major towns and cities to advance to Minas Tirith (Midsummer) for the wedding festivities.\n2\tTalk to Rodwen up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tRodwen is up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Rodwen has asked to meet you outside the throne room, and away from listening ears. For what purpose does the expert wedding-planner seek this secret meeting?\n",
[1849]="7002093C\n1\tTalk to Elrohir at Thorenhad\tElrohir is at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond, north of the Bruinen Gorges in the Trollshaws. Pethelen has suggested a first step for your urgent errand: a visit with Elrohir at Thorenhad for an introduction to Radanir, one of the Dúnedain currently staying at Thorenhad.\n2\tTalk to Elweleth at Thorenhad\tElweleth is by the horses at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond in the Trollshaws. Elrohir has told you to speak with Elweleth, for she will know where Radanir the Ranger has gone, if anyone will.\n3\tTalk to Radanir\tRadanir is at the Laenan cave system, located in the north-west reaches of the Gladdalf, the wood-troll infested marshes of the North Trollshaws. You have spoken with Elweleth at Thorenhad, and she told you where to find Radanir the Dúnadan.\n4\tDefeat Laenan Orc-warriors (total: 8)\030Defeat Laenan Orc-defilers (total: 4)\030Defeat Laenan Orc-leader\tOrc-warriors, Orc-defilers, and their leaders can be found within the confusing network of tunnels known as Laenan. Radanir has agreed to join the Grey Company on its journey south to aid Aragorn, but he wants you to deal with the Orc raiding-party he tracked through the Trollshaws.\n5\tTalk to Elrohir at Thorenhad\tElrohir is at Thorenhad, his camp in the Trollshaws. You have given Radanir the message for which you sought him, and he has agreed to join the Grey Company on its journey south. You should return to Elrohir now that you have dealt with the Orc raiding-party in the Laenan caves.\n",
[1850]="70061BC9\n1\tTalk to Tegwyn in the alley between buildings in Mossward\tTegwyn has overheard much of your conversation concerning Saruman and the Uruks.\n2\tTalk to Meneldir in the alley between buildings in Mossward\tMeneldir is in an alley between buildings in Mossward.\n3\tSearch for a sign of the Uruks where the road enters Swanfleet from Enedwaith\tThe road runs north-east past Mossward and on into Enedwaith. Did the Uruks come from that direction?\n4\tExamine one of the dead Uruks along the road\tThe bodies of Uruks lie on the road where it enters Swanfleet from Enedwaith.\n5\tCollect fallen Uruk swords along the road from Enedwaith (total: 3)\tMeneldir will want to examine the weapons carried by these Uruks.\n6\tBring the Uruk swords to Meneldir in the Mossward town square\tMeneldir is in the Mossward town square, waiting for you to return with news of the border with Enedwaith.\n7\tBring the Uruk swords to Skardí Bendblade inside his shop in Mossward\tSkardí Bendblade will be interested in the Uruk swords you recovered. Skardí is always hard at work in his Mossward shop.\n",
[1851]="7003FD4C\n1\tTalk to Darláf at the south-east road\030Talk to Bosa at the eastern camp-fire\030Talk to Sídrac by the encampment's supplier\tDarláf, Sídrac, and Bosa can be found at the encampment in Dunharrow, south of Éowyn's position. Éowyn has asked you to comfort some of the Men at the encampment in Dunharrow, for they heard of Aragorn's departure and have begun to question the wisdom of Théoden's ride to Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to Éowyn at the camp in Dunharrow\tÉowyn is at the muster of the Rohirrim, at Dunharrow. You have spoken with some worried soldiers of the camp, and should return now to Éowyn.\n3\tTalk to Radwine at the camp in Dunharrow, by Éowyn\tRadwine is speaking to Éowyn at the camp in Dunharrow.\n",
[1852]="70000179\n1\tTalk to Strider\tStrider is in his room at The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree, which is found by taking a left down the hall out of the common room until you can only bear right. The room is at the end of the hall to the right of the stairs. At night-fall, Strider will lead you against Amdir and the Blackwolds.\n2\tTalk to Strider\tStrider is in his room at The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree, which is found by taking a left down the hall out of the common room until you can only bear right. The room is at the end of the hall to the right of the stairs. With the threat of Amdir ended, you should report back to Strider and see if there is anything else he would have you do.\n",
[1853]="700579E8\n1\tBring the letters of introduction to Isteron in the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tIsteron is outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Rodwen gave you some letters of introduction authorizing you to act on her behalf, and directed you to deliver them to her friend and ally Isteron.\n2\tFind the helpful hobbits south of the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tTwo of the helpful hobbits that helped Isteron with some of the wedding preparations are relaxing nearby: Frodo Baggins and Samwise Gamgee!\n3\tTalk to Frodo Baggins in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to Samwise Gamgee in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tTwo of the helpful hobbits that helped Isteron with some of the wedding preparations are relaxing nearby: Frodo Baggins and Samwise Gamgee!\n4\tFollow the smell of pipe-smoke to the south-west in order to find Merry and Pippin\tFrodo and Sam suggested that you follow the smell of pipe-smoke to find Merry and Pippin. Frodo and Sam provided some very helpful advice to Rodwen's wedding-planning friends, but Merry and Pippin seemed very amused about something, which strikes young Master Samwise as perhaps a troubling sign.\n5\tFollow the smell of pipe-smoke to the south-east in order to find Merry and Pippin\tFrodo and Sam suggested that you follow the smell of pipe-smoke to find Merry and Pippin. Frodo and Sam provided some very helpful advice to Rodwen's wedding-planning friends, but Merry and Pippin seemed very amused about something, which strikes young Master Samwise as perhaps a troubling sign.\n6\tTalk to Meriadoc Brandybuck in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMerry is atop the wall south-east of the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), very pleased with some recent mischief.\n7\tTalk to Peregrin Took in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tPippin is atop the wall south-east of the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), very pleased with some recent mischief.\n8\tExamine the fruit of the hobbit's mischief at the base of the ramp from the Seventh Circle, in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tMerry and Pippin, quite delighted with themselves, have caused some mischief. You should find Cúfaron at the base of the ramp from the Seventh Circle, in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer), and see if it is too late to undo their handiwork.\n9\tTalk to Legolas in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tLegolas stands by the pile of blue decorations, and despite his solemn expression you can tell he is also rather amused at the hobbits' prank.\n10\tTalk to Cúfaron in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\tCúfaron is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n",
[1854]="70061BCB\n1\tTalk to Tegwyn inside the Mossward blacksmith shop\tTegwyn has been bothering Skardí Bendblade all morning, and the blacksmith wants you to do something about him.\n2\tCollect boar tusks along the Old South Road (total: 8)\030Collect craban talons along the Old South Road (total: 4)\030Collect potential whetstones along the Old South Road (total: 6)\tSkardí Bendblade asked you to collect boar tusks, craban talons, and potential whetstones he might put to various uses for the town.\n3\tBring the tusks, talons, and potential whetstones to Skardí Bendblade in his shop\tSkardí Bendblade is waiting in his shop in Mossward for the items you collected.\n4\tSkardí Bendblade told you that Tegwyn never returned to his home, and you should check the perimeter of the town for the missing boy.\t\n5\tTalk to Merion by the east gate of Mossward\tYou should tell one of the nearby town guards that Tegwyn is missing from Mossward.\n",
[1855]="7003FD6E\n1\tTalk to Radwine at Dunharrow and he will bring you to the Paths of the Dead\tRadwine is at the camp in Dunharrow, by Éowyn. Radwine has asked you to dare the darkness of the Paths of the Dead in search of his friend Elfdag.\n2\tTalk to Elfdag at the camp in Dunharrow\tYou rescued Elfdag from the Paths of the Dead and should speak to him at the camp in Dunharrow.\n3\tTalk to Éowyn at the camp in Dunharrow\tÉowyn is at the encampment in Dunharrow.\n",
[1856]="7000017A\n1\tTalk to Constable Underhill\tConstable Underhill often loiters about Combe town centre, east and north of Bree. Strider has informed you that he has an important matter to attend to, but has asked you to go to Combe and encourage Constable Underhill to investigate the brigands' old hideout.\n",
})
